  "meta": {
    "title": "The Mountain Closest to Space Is NOT Everest 🏔️🚀🤯",
    "description": "Everest 🇳🇵 is the highest mountain above sea level at 8,849 m, but it's not the point closest to space! 🚀 Earth isn't a perfect ball: it's thicker at the equator. Chimborazo in Ecuador 🇪🇨 is only 6,263 m high, but it sits just one degree south of the equator, on top of that bulge. Its summit is 6,384.4 km from Earth's center, about 2.1 km farther out than Everest's 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "The closest point to space is in Ecuador, not Nepal 🤯🇪🇨",
      "Did you know Earth is fatter at the equator? 👇",
      "Which record should we explain next? 🗺️"
    ],
